{"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["Trees"]}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"externalID":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV12GraphDrawingE21reingoldTilfordLayoutAD0E0VyxGyF","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reingoldTilfordLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()","extendedModule":"Trees","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift#L37"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The root is at (0, 0) and a vertex at depth d has y = d. Children are placed left to right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, vertices at one depth at least 1 apart along each subtree’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contour, and every parent centred over its first and last child. Where two subtrees had to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be pushed apart, the smaller subtrees between them are spaced evenly (Walker’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"improvement), so a mirrored tree draws as the reflection of the drawing and isomorphic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subtrees are drawn identically up to translation. Coordinates are "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" arithmetic:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separations and centring alone give multiples of a power of ½, which are exact, but the even"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spacing divides a shift by the number of gaps it is spread over, so values such as ±5\/6"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"occur and are rounded (and a mirrored tree’s drawing then matches the reflection only to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rounding)."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reingold and Tilford, “Tidier drawings of trees”, IEEE Transactions on Software"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Engineering SE-7(2), 1981."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Walker, “A node-positioning algorithm for general trees”, Software: Practice and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Experience 20(7), 1990."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert, “Improving Walker’s algorithm to run in linear time”,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Graph Drawing (GD 2002), LNCS 2528, 2002."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n) time and memory, with no recursion."}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The tidy drawing of the tree: Reingold and Tilford’s layered tree drawing as Walker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refined it, in Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert’s linear-time form.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree\/reingoldtilfordlayout()"]}],"references":{"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees","title":"Trees"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Drawing":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A position in the plane for each vertex, in a fixed vertex order: what every layout in this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module returns, and what a caller passes as a starting drawing."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/drawing","kind":"symbol","title":"Drawing","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees/RootedTree/reingoldTilfordLayout()":{"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"t